      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/f07891/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-07-03T06:03:58.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I posted this on BGG, but thought I might get a quicker, more accurate reponse here.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>Ok so I was trying this out solo, playing two Strike force ships (Vigilance, Ranak Warbeast).</span><br><br><span>Let me see if I can describe what happened. The start of the game I placed the opp. ships 1-2-1 (Technovore). My forces attacked and destroyed the opp ship in the right sector. During Aftermath a mission card had an Aftermath event that brought out an opp. ship to the center (now totally 3). This now caused the sector to be overrun(we had to flip 3 station cards. My understanding is that since the ship came out during the aftermath event phase it is considered unengaged so we merit a station card flip (this i may have got wrong). This triggered the Technovore Flagship to enter play.&nbsp;</span><br><br><span>As the next round began a travel event in the sector with the flagship instructed me to move the ship with the most [E] to the sector with the fewest ships, so with 2 opp. ships in one sector and my two strike force ships in the either .. we chose to move the flagship into our sector.</span><br><br><span>Through some great cards I was able to install tech and use boosts to get Vigilance attack to sixteen .. more than enough to wipe out the Hive Master ...&nbsp;</span><br><br><span>we easily won on round 2 ... did I miss something?</span></p>",
